  "term": "dressing apraxia",
  "definition": "Dressing apraxia is a form of apraxia in which a person cannot carry out the previously learned act of putting on clothes even though the problem is not due to basic motor or sensory loss. It reflects difficulty mentally organizing the actions needed for dressing.",
